    <h2 id="d-c-h">Selected</h2>
    <h3>BCG Jeel Tamooh Fellowship</h3>
    <p>Boston Consulting Group’s flagship six-month leadership program for Saudi Arabia’s most promising university students. I’m one of about 150 fellows in its 8th edition, selected from the Kingdom’s top universities.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>One-on-one mentorship.</b> Paired with a BCG consultant for personalized guidance and career support throughout the program.</li>
      <li><b>The consulting toolkit.</b> Consulting Taster Workshops on BCG’s structured problem-solving methodology: hypothesis-driven case thinking, analytical reasoning and executive communication, practiced in team-based exercises.</li>
      <li><b>Sectors shaping Vision 2030.</b> Expert-led sessions on megatrends like AI, automation and geopolitical shifts, and on sectors such as fintech and sustainability.</li>
      <li><b>From ambition to a plan.</b> Workshops with BCG consultants and alumni that turn career goals into a concrete roadmap with clear objectives and accountability.</li>
      <li><b>A blended format.</b> Virtual learning modules combined with in-person workshops and engagements.</li>
      <li><b>Access.</b> Networking with BCG partners, consultants and recruiters, and preparation for consulting interview processes, including BCG’s visiting associate pathway.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>KAUST Academy AI Specialization</h3>
    <p>A four-stage program with an assessment after every stage. Around 7,000 students applied. About 500 reach the advanced stage, which is where I made it. The stages I completed:</p>
    <ul><li>Prerequisites: Python and the math behind machine learning.</li><li>Introduction to AI: classical ML, neural networks and PyTorch.</li><li>Advanced AI: computer vision with convolutional networks.</li></ul>
